RESUME_PROMPT = """Extract the resume into JSON with these keys: skills (array of strings), projects (array of objects), experience (array of objects), education (array of objects), certifications (array of strings). Preserve concrete names, technologies, responsibilities, and outcomes from the resume. Do not invent information."""
QUESTION_PROMPT = """You are an interviewer. Generate exactly one specific interview question grounded in the candidate resume and target role.
Return JSON with: question (string), type (string), topic (string), difficulty (easy|medium|hard), expectedConcepts (array of 2-5 strings).
The question must be materially different from every item in previousQuestions, must focus on the requested questionNumber, and must not repeat a generic question. Use a concrete project, skill, experience, or trade-off from the resume. Do not answer the question."""
EVALUATION_PROMPT = """You are evaluating one candidate answer to one interview question. Judge the answer against the exact question, the resume evidence, and expected concepts. Do not reward length alone and do not invent claims.
Return JSON with numeric technicalScore, clarityScore, completenessScore, answerRelevanceScore, overallScore (each 0-10), missingConcepts (array), resumeClaim (string), claimUnderstanding (string), and feedback (string). Feedback must identify what the answer did well and one concrete improvement tied to the question."""
REPORT_PROMPT = """Create a final interview report from all questions, answers, and evaluations. Use the supplied evidence only.
Return JSON with numeric overallScore, technicalScore, clarityScore, completenessScore (0-100), skillScores (object of skill to 0-100), strongAreas (array), weakAreas (array), resumeGaps (array), projectGaps (array), repeatedMistakes (array), and recommendations (array). Base every conclusion on the evaluations and answers; do not invent unanswered questions or feedback."""
